osed mainly of  fibrofatty and contains a single nodule  0 4 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm   which is grossly  consistent with a fibroadenoma  There are no areas that are grossly  suspicious for invasive carcinoma  A specimen radiograph was performed and  breast fragments containing microcalcifications were submitted as noted below   Micro  1  Breast with microcalcification  ESS  2 frags  1 cass   Micros  2 3  Other calcified areas by specimen radiograph  ESS  5 frags  2  cass   Micros  4 9  Remainder of breast biopsy  ESS  11 frags  6 cass   The second specimen  labelled  axillary node   consists of a 3 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  fragment of fibrofatty with a REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm encapsulated hemorrhagic area and a  0 5 x 0 6cm gray gritty area  A portion of the tissue has been saved for snap  freeze and possibly ERICA analysis   Micro  10  Axillary node  1 frag  1 cass   Reports to  MATORY  YVEDT M D   SPECIMEN TYPE  BREAST BIOPSY W O MARGINS  ADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE  LYMPH NODE FOR HEMATOPATHOLOGY WORKUP   report_end  , Absent.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Corrected Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  06 MAY 96 ACCESSIONED ON  06 MAY 96 at 13 31 CLINICAL DATA  Mass in left breast                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 1  REMOVED_DATE CM EXTENDING TO THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN IN SMALL FOCI  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU CONFINED TO THE REGION OF THE MASS  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  08 MAY 96 at 15 22                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  11 MAY 96 at 10 10     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     THIS ADDENDUM HAS BEEN DELETED FOR THIS REPORT GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh  in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast tissue  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm firm piece of breast tissue  Inked and sectioned to reveal a 2 0cm gritty white mass extending to multiple inked margins  Representative section is frozen as FX 1 and saved frozen  The remainder is submitted in A through E  Resident  Joseph Misdraji  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA ASSOCIATED WITH CALCIFICATIONS  O R  Resident  Jacqueline Haas  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Max L  Goodman  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Wiley W Souba Jr   M D  PART   LEFT BREAST BIOPSY   report_end  , Present.
