Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  12 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  12 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 11 50 CLINICAL DATA  Status post right mastectomy                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LET   BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL ADENOCARCINOMA  95    POORLY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE 3 3   EXTENDING TO THE RESECTION MARGINS AND INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  5    CRIBRIFORM TYPE  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The tumor is 0 5cm in size  There is focal perineural invasion  No vascular or lymphatic invasion is identified  Diagnosis by  Austin L  Vickery  M D  Signed On  14 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 15 11                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FROZEN TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  the results of prospective staining for estrogen receptor protein of 100 unfixed breast tumors were compared with determinations of estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  93  of tumors that reacted with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  100  of tumors that failed to stain were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining for progesterone receptor protein of 50 breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Seventy three percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 91  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL 