n is marked with blue ink  the posterior margin with black ink  the superior margin with green ink  and the inferior margin with yellow ink  The specimen is serially sectioned from the lateral to the medial aspect  The larger component  which occupies the lateral half of the specimen  consists mainly of soft  lobulated  yellow tan adipose tissue  The smaller component  which comprises the medial half of the specimen  consists mainly of soft  focally cystic  white fibrous tissue  The specimen is entirely submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  from the lateral to the medial aspect with the area of calcifications in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Gross Dictation by Tim Robinson  on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Kristina Braaten M D   on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Kristina Braaten M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART   BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION , Absent.
