Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  23 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  24 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 10 13 CLINICAL DATA  Forty seven year old with incidentally found left breast nodule  Biopsy showed extensive ductal carcinoma in situ                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT  AND ADDITIONAL AXILLARY CONTENTS  MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  INFILTRATING  40   AND INTRADUCTAL  60   CARCINOMA  MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE II III   SEE NOTE  NOTE  The examined inked resection margins are free of carcinoma  Lymphatic invasion is not seen  Carcinoma is present in five of six slides of breast  Nipple is unremarkable  Fourteen of fourteen axillary lymph nodes are free of tumor  Diagnosis by  Eugene Jerome Mark  M D  Signed On  01 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 16 54                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  12 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 14 29     ADDITIONAL DIAGNOSTIC INFORMATION Addendum     The residual tumor size is greater than 2cm in overall extent  Because of the multifocal nature of the carcinoma  a more accurate size cannot be expressed  No gross lesion was present  Added by  Eugene Jerome Mark  M D  Signed On  15 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 14 30 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in two containers  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  Labeled  left breast  is a 22 x 18 x 4 8cm left breast with an attached 7 x 6 x 1 5cm portion of axillary tissue  The contained skin with unremarkable nipple measures REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm  with a 6cm in length well healed scar along the superior margin  Two sutures are in place  a long suture laterally and a short suture superiorly  The axillary tissue contains multiple firm and enlarged lymph nodes  tan red on cut section and measuring up to 2 1cm in length  The breast parenchyma contains multiple confluent areas of linear tan gray firm tissue streaks  the largest confluent area REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm  This confluent area contains cystic spaces filled with soft  yellow tan material  There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm area of more red colored fibrous tissue  located medially and just beneath the medial border of the skin scar  No discrete biopsy cavity is noted  No discrete nodules are noted  The area of red colored fibrous tissue extends to within 2 5cm of the nearest margin  which is deep  Received fresh in a container  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  additional axillary tissue  is a 2 5cm in diameter aggregate of fibroadipose tissue which contains two fragmented lymph nodes  tan pink in color and measuring from REMOVED_DATE to 1 0cm in length  Section Code A   lymph nodes   additional axillary   2 B E   axillary tail lymph nodes  main specimen F   nipple and skin scar G H   red colored fibrous tissue  possible previous biopsy site I J   fibrous tissue with cystic areas containing soft tan material K M   representative breast tissue Resident  Kathleen K  Hansen  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  Michael J Yaremchuk  M D  PART A  POSITIONAL AXILLARY TISSUE PART B  LEFT BREAST and AXILLARY CONTENTS   report_end  , Present.
